change:
  id: CHG-010
  title: Route the evolution loop through an interchangeable agent harness
  status: proposed
  intent: Connect the provider-neutral AgentHarness boundary to the live evolution loop while retaining retrieval context and deterministic candidate authority.
  relates_to:
    - ARCH-001
    - Q-010
    - Q-011

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: harness-driven-evolution
    requirement: The evolution loop can use an ACP-backed AgentHarness as its proposer and still perform validation, candidate realization, checks, scoring and promotion recording through the existing deterministic path.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: the acp profile is configured and the harness completes with a mutation
        then: the mutation is evaluated by the normal candidate/check/fitness path
        and:
          - the prepared retrieval bundle is available to the harness request
          - the harness result is treated as a proposal, never as approval
          - the route and resource budget are supplied at the adapter boundary
      - id: S2
        when: the harness fails, times out, rejects or returns no mutation
        then: no candidate is created and the run fails with bounded evidence
      - id: S3
        when: the ACP profile is configured with explicit command and resource properties
        then: command arguments and bounded request budget are resolved at the adapter edge
acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: adapters/evolve/EvolveRunnerTest.routesPreparedRetrievalThroughAnAgentHarnessBeforeDeterministicEvaluation
    layer: component
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: adapters/evolve/AgentHarnessMutationProposerTest.rejectsNonCompletedRunsBeforeCandidateCreation
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: adapters/evolve/AgentHarnessMutationProposerTest.returnsCompletedMutationAndExposesRouteEvidence
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/acp/AcpAgentConfigTest.readsCommandArgumentsAndResourceBudgetFromExplicitProperties
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: adapt prepared proposal requests to AgentRequest without leaking provider types
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: compose ACP into the proposer profile registry and live EvolveRunner path
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: prove successful harness routing, route evidence and non-completed failure semantics
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: exercise installed OpenCode, Goose, Codex or Claude ACP commands in an opt-in environment
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - automatic provider selection based on complexity or remaining credits
  - automatic merge or production deployment
  - provider-specific types in domain or deterministic
  - trusting an agent result as a fitness or promotion decision

risks:
  - ACP agent implementations differ in tool permissions and output discipline; the disposable proposal workspace limits accidental target mutation, and real-engine coverage is opt-in
  - ACP reports wall-clock usage only; token and credit values can be configured and preflight-checked but remain policy inputs until provider usage is exposed
  - ACP argument configuration is intentionally whitespace-separated and does not implement shell quoting
